  "problem": "Find the solutions **in radians** to the equation $\\operatorname{tan}\u2061x=\\frac{3}{2}$ for $0\\le x<2\\pi .$ Round your answers to **one decimal place**.\n\n**In ascending order,** the solutions are $x=$\n{{field-1}}\nand $x=$ \n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\nx=arctan\\,(\\frac{3}{2})=0.982\\,793\u2026\u22481.0\n$$\n\nSince $1.0$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}=1.0.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of $\\pi .$ Hence,\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=\\pi +0.982\\,793\u2026\u22484.1.\n$$\n\nSo, in ascending order and rounded to one decimal place, the solutions are $x=1.0$ and $x=4.1.$",
